                "Let T(n) be the number of terms computed (calls made). One call for this n, plus the calls of its two children: <b>T(n) = T(n − 1) + T(n − 2) + 1</b>, with T(0) = T(1) = 1 ‡.",
                "Slide 1.60's table follows from that:<ul><li>T(2) = 1 + 1 + 1 = 3</li><li>T(3) = 3 + 1 + 1 = 5</li><li>T(4) = 5 + 3 + 1 = 9</li><li>T(5) = 9 + 5 + 1 = 15</li><li>T(6) = 15 + 9 + 1 = 25</li></ul>",
