              "Take n a power of 2 and draw each call with the work it does itself.<br>1. Level d has 2<sup>d</sup> nodes, each of size n/2<sup>d</sup> and cost c·n/2<sup>d</sup>.<br>2. So level d costs 2<sup>d</sup> × c·n/2<sup>d</sup> = cn.<br>3. Sizes reach 1 when n/2<sup>h</sup> = 1, so h = lg n.<br>4. There are 2<sup>lg n</sup> = n leaves of cost Θ(1), together Θ(n).<br>5. T(n) = cn lg n + Θ(n) = <b>Θ(n lg n)</b>.<br>The splitting and merging do not depend on the key values, so this holds in every case.",
