              "• <b>Method 1 (Iterative Loop: $\\Theta(n)$ Time)</b>:<br><code>sum = 0; for (i = 1; i &lt;= n; i++) sum += i;</code>: Executes $n$ additions, so $T(n) = \\mathbf{\\Theta(n)}$.<br>• <b>Method 2 (Closed-Form Gauss Formula: $\\Theta(1)$ Time)</b>:<br><code>sum = n * (n + 1) / 2;</code>: Executes 1 addition, 1 multiplication, and 1 division (3 arithmetic operations regardless of $n$), so $T(n) = \\mathbf{\\Theta(1)}$.<br><i>(Bonus Method 3, Algorithm B on slide 2.57: a nested loop adding 1, $n - i + 1$ times in pass $i$, takes $n(n+1)/2 = \\Theta(n^2)$ time.)</i>",
