              "• <b>Q3</b> ($n^{\\log_2 4} = n^2$): (A) Case 1 $\\implies \\mathbf{\\Theta(n^2)}$; (B) Case 2 $\\implies \\mathbf{\\Theta(n^2 \\lg n)}$; (C) Case 3 $\\implies \\mathbf{\\Theta(n^3)}$.<br>• <b>Q4</b>: $T(8) = 4T(1) + 2(8) = 4(50) + 16 = 216$; $T(64) = 4T(8) + 2(64) = 4(216) + 128 = 864 + 128 = \\mathbf{992}$.",
