                "A power of a fraction applies to both parts: (a/b)<sup>n</sup> = a<sup>n</sup> / b<sup>n</sup>. Example: (5/3)<sup>2</sup> = 25/9. The induction proof below uses exactly this.",
                "Common trap: 2<sup>n</sup> · 2<sup>n</sup> = 2<sup>2n</sup> = 4<sup>n</sup>, not 2<sup>n²</sup>. And 2<sup>2n</sup> is much smaller than 2<sup>2ⁿ</sup>, where the exponent is itself a power.",
