                "The slides' pivot rule (Lecture 5): the pivot is the <b>first</b> element of the range, x = A[p].",
                "<code>RAND-PARTITION</code> first swaps a uniformly random element of A[p .. q] into position p, then runs the same PARTITION. So every element of the range is the pivot with the same probability 1/(q − p + 1).",
