          "<b>Naive $\\Theta(m + n)$ Algorithm</b>:<br>1. Use the two-finger <code>MERGE</code> procedure from Merge Sort to merge the two sorted arrays <code>A[0..m-1]</code> and <code>B[0..n-1]</code> into a single sorted array <code>C[0..m+n-1]</code> in $\\Theta(m + n)$ time.<br>2. Let $N = m + n$. If $N$ is odd, return <code>C[N // 2]</code>; if $N$ is even, return the lower median <code>C[N // 2 - 1]</code> (or average <code>(C[N//2 - 1] + C[N//2]) / 2.0</code>).<br><i>Space-optimized $\\Theta(m+n)$ time, $O(1)$ space variant</i>: Advance two pointers <code>i</code> (in <code>A</code>) and <code>j</code> (in <code>B</code>) exactly $\\lfloor(m+n)/2\\rfloor$ steps without allocating <code>C</code>.",
