          "<b>Naive $O(nm)$ Wildcard Pattern Matching Algorithm</b>:<br><pre>vector&lt;int&gt; findMatches(string S, string P) {\n  int n = S.length(), m = P.length();\n  vector&lt;int&gt; M;\n  for (int j = 0; j &lt;= n - m; j++) {\n    bool match = true;\n    for (int k = 0; k &lt; m; k++) {\n      if (P[k] != '*' &amp;&amp; P[k] != S[j + k]) {\n        match = false;\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n    if (match) M.push_back(j);\n  }\n  return M; // Naturally sorted in increasing order of j\n}</pre><b>Complexity</b>: Outer loop runs $n - m + 1 = O(n)$ times; inner loop runs at most $m$ comparisons per shift $j \\implies \\mathbf{O(nm)}$ time.",
