            "Base-case trap: T(n) ≤ c lg n cannot hold at n = 1, because lg 1 = 0 and T(1) &gt; 0. That is why the O definition (Asymptotic section below) says \"for all n ≥ n<sub>0</sub>\", where n<sub>0</sub> is the point from which the bound must hold: you may start at n<sub>0</sub> = 2 instead."
