            "Slide 3.4 example: <b>√n = Ω(lg n)</b> with c = 1, n<sub>0</sub> = 16.<ul><li>n = 16: √16 = 4 and lg 16 = 4, so 4 ≥ 4 holds.</li><li>n = 64: 8 ≥ 6 holds.</li><li>n = 8: 2.83 ≥ 3 fails, which is allowed because 8 is below n<sub>0</sub>.</li></ul>",
