            "Three outcomes, slide 3.24: f(n) is smaller, or larger, by a polynomial factor n<sup>ε</sup>, or f(n) is asymptotically equal to n<sup>log<sub>b</sub> a</sup>. Asymptotically equal means f(n) = Θ(n<sup>log<sub>b</sub> a</sup>): the same size up to a constant factor. The table states the three cases exactly as on slide 3.25.",
