          "Compute Fibonacci of 16 in four steps only and show the details of your answer (Midterm 2024 Q6 & Midterm 2025 Q4).",
          "Let M = $\\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix}$, and use M<sup>n</sup> = $\\begin{pmatrix}F_{n+1}&F_n\\\\F_n&F_{n-1}\\end{pmatrix}$. Since 16 = 2<sup>4</sup>, four squarings are enough.<br>1. M<sup>2</sup> = $\\begin{pmatrix}1+1&1+0\\\\1+0&1+0\\end{pmatrix}$ = $\\begin{pmatrix}2&1\\\\1&1\\end{pmatrix}$.<br>2. M<sup>4</sup> = (M<sup>2</sup>)<sup>2</sup> = $\\begin{pmatrix}4+1&2+1\\\\2+1&1+1\\end{pmatrix}$ = $\\begin{pmatrix}5&3\\\\3&2\\end{pmatrix}$.<br>3. M<sup>8</sup> = (M<sup>4</sup>)<sup>2</sup> = $\\begin{pmatrix}25+9&15+6\\\\15+6&9+4\\end{pmatrix}$ = $\\begin{pmatrix}34&21\\\\21&13\\end{pmatrix}$.<br>4. M<sup>16</sup> = (M<sup>8</sup>)<sup>2</sup> = $\\begin{pmatrix}1156+441&714+273\\\\714+273&441+169\\end{pmatrix}$ = $\\begin{pmatrix}1597&987\\\\987&610\\end{pmatrix}$.<br>The top-right entry is <b>F(16) = 987</b>.",
