          "Invariant before each iteration: A[p] = x, A[p+1..i] ≤ x, A[i+1..j−1] ≥ x, A[j..q] unexamined.<br><b>Initialization.</b> i = p and j = p + 1: both regions are empty, so true.<br><b>Maintenance.</b> If A[j] &gt; x, it joins the ≥ region when j grows. If A[j] ≤ x: i grows by one and A[i] ↔ A[j] puts the small value in the ≤ region and moves the old ≥ value to the end of the ≥ region. True again.<br><b>Termination.</b> j = q + 1: A[p+1..i] ≤ x and A[i+1..q] ≥ x. The final exchange A[p] ↔ A[i] puts x between them. The array is correctly partitioned.",
