            "Usual choice (Slide 8.82): hash1(key) = key % TABLE_SIZE, and hash2(key) = PRIME − (key % PRIME), where PRIME is a prime smaller than TABLE_SIZE. Since key % PRIME is 0 to PRIME − 1, hash2 is 1 to PRIME: never 0.",
